{"name":"Hell’s Bells","hex":"#ba622a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place of torment where some or all sinners are believed to go after death and evil spirits are believed to be.","Synonym of underworld, an underground land of the dead without eternal punishment or with only some regions of punishment."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or situation of great suffering in life.","A place for gambling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hell"},{"term":"bells","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bell"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ship's bells; the strokes on a ship's bell, every half-hour, to mark the passage of time.","Ellipsis of bell-bottoms."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bells"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hell","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, Hell is a location or state in the afterlife in which souls are subjected to punishment after death. Religions with a linear divine history sometimes depict hells as eternal, such as in some versions of Christianity and Islam, whereas religions with reincarnation usually depict a hell as an intermediary period between incarnations, as is the case in the Indian religions. Religions typically locate Hell in another dimension or under Earth's surface. Other afterlife destinations include heaven, paradise, purgatory, limbo, and the underworld."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/330px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell","wikidata":"Q564"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg/500px-Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg/500px-Hel_%281889%29_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hel (1889) by Johannes Gehrts, depicts the Old Norse Hel, a goddess-like figure, in the location of the same name, which she oversees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHel_(1889)_by_Johannes_Gehrts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG/500px-Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG/1280px-Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG/500px-Fresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Preserved colonial wall paintings of 1802 depicting Hell,[14][15][16] by Tadeo Escalante, inside the Church of San Juan Bautista in Huaro, Peru","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresque_%C3%A9glise_huaro.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg/500px-Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg/1280px-Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg/500px-Dumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ancient Sumerian cylinder seal impression showing the god Dumuzid being tortured in the Underworld by galla demons","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADumuzi_aux_enfers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.